# Upstream sources this image vendors, pinned. Renovate drives every value
# here; the regex managers that read them live in renovate.json.
#
# After either ref moves, run scripts/sync-upstream.sh to refresh
# migrations/10-init-scripts and migrations/20-migrations. CI re-runs that
# script and fails the PR if the vendored SQL does not match these pins, so a
# Renovate bump cannot land without the SQL it implies.

# Supabase's schema: the four init-scripts plus the dbmate migration set.
#
# Pinned to a release tag rather than a branch. Note the tag list also carries
# build artefacts (`-amchecktest`, `-orioledb-*`, `-x86`) and at least one
# malformed entry (17.6.1.15799999); renovate.json filters both, so only clean
# four-part versions are ever proposed.
# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=supabase/postgres versioning=regex:^(?<major>\d+)\.(?<minor>\d+)\.(?<patch>\d+)\.(?<build>\d+)$
SUPABASE_POSTGRES_REF=17.11.0.001

# The self-host-only SQL (roles/jwt/webhooks/realtime/_supabase) lives in the
# supabase/supabase monorepo under docker/volumes/db, which has no release of
# its own. Pinned by commit so builds stay reproducible; Renovate advances the
# digest as master moves.
# renovate: datasource=git-refs depName=https://github.com/supabase/supabase
SUPABASE_DOCKER_BRANCH=master
SUPABASE_DOCKER_SHA=bd43802d7b4daa777d55f3b9b01e9062c7988dc0
